{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ec7e39d99b57bc5ac1", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Thermodynamics - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a8f"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a4a", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29e3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475d"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4713"], "question": {"text": "Given are statements for certain thermodynamic variables,\n(A) Internal energy, volume (V) and mass (M) are extensive variables.\n(B) Pressure (P), temperature (T) and density ( $\\rho$ ) are intensive variables.\n(C) Volume (V), temperature (T) and density ( $\\rho$ ) are intensive variables.\n(D) Mass (M), temperature (T) and internal energy are extensive variables.\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "fe74df", "text": "(B) and (C) Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29e4"}, {"id": "c825a2", "text": "(C) and (D) Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29e5"}, {"id": "0fc4f1", "text": "(D) and (A) Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29e6"}, {"id": "cda700", "text": "(A) and (B) Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29e7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29e8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4739"], "question": {"text": "Half mole of an ideal monoatomic gas is heated at a constant pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>atm</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. Work done by the gas is<math><mo>(</mo></math>Gas constant,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.21</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "9f1f8d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>73</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29e9"}, {"id": "ee3a3e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>581</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29ea"}, {"id": "ad9c78", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>291</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29eb"}, {"id": "375001", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>146</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29ec"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29ed", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e808d"], "question": {"text": "<p>The given figure represents two isobaric processes for the same mass of an ideal gas, then</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F05dc0f9f-f20a-49af-8454-c5508d494c0a.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 200px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "685d07", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29ee"}, {"id": "b29b45", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29ef"}, {"id": "894bf3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29f0"}, {"id": "fd99f2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29f1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29f2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["6176f3e76581241c7072a032"], "concepts": ["6176f3f46581241c7072ae97"], "question": {"text": "The entropy of any system is given by,&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>ln</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>kR</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> are the constants. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> are number of moles, mechanical equivalent of heat, Boltzmann&#39;s constant and gas constant, respectively.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mtext>Take&#160;</mtext><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Choose the incorrect option from the following:"}, "options": [{"id": "869b43", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>J</mi></math> have the same dimensions.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29f3"}, {"id": "341064", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>R</mi></math> have the same dimensions.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29f4"}, {"id": "68ff95", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> have different dimensions.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29f5"}, {"id": "8a6e0a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> have the same dimensions.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29f6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29f7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba3"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of a liquid is converted to vapour at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Pa</mi></math> pressure. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the heat supplied is used for increasing the volume by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;during this phase change, then the increase in internal energy in the process will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "c3b176", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4320</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29f8"}, {"id": "ea59a9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>432000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29f9"}, {"id": "781055", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29fa"}, {"id": "79d749", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29fb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29fc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "A balloon filled with helium&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>and</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>1</mn><mo>.7</mo><mi>atm</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;bursts. Immediately after wards the expansion of helium can be considered as :&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "27fd7c", "text": "irreversible isothermal", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29fd"}, {"id": "5c8990", "text": "irreversible adiabatic", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29fe"}, {"id": "ac4344", "text": "reversible adiabatic", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f29ff"}, {"id": "0695ce", "text": "reversible isothermal", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a00"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a01", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475d"], "concepts": ["6162fb026ed13040ec84a08f"], "question": {"text": "There are two vessels filled with an ideal gas where volume of one is double the volume of other. The large vessel contains the gas at 8 kPa at 1000 K while the smaller vessel contains the gas at 7 kPa at 500 K. If the vessels are connected to each other by a thin tube allowing the gas to flow and the temperature of both vessels is maintained at 600 K , at steady state the pressure in the vessels will be (in kPa)."}, "options": [{"id": "1f8a6b", "text": "$4.4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a02"}, {"id": "5377a7", "text": "$6$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a03"}, {"id": "8b2e93", "text": "$24$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a04"}, {"id": "1bc882", "text": "$18$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a05"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a06", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["6176f3e76581241c7072a032"], "concepts": ["6176f3f46581241c7072ae97"], "question": {"text": "An ideal gas in a cylinder is separated by a piston in such a way that the entropy of one part is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and that of the other part is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. Given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. If the piston is removed then the total entropy of the system will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "56664d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a07"}, {"id": "7bbb3b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a08"}, {"id": "3e3489", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a09"}, {"id": "28d7b4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a0a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a0b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0f1"], "question": {"text": "<p>A sample of an ideal gas is taken through the cyclic process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math> as shown in figure. It absorbs, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of heat during the part <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>, no heat during <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> and rejects <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of heat during <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math>. A work of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> is done on the gas during the part <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. The internal energy of the gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1560</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. The work done by the gas during the part <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math> is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa34d352d-82ef-450a-a47a-09a0cf5845cc-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "da25f2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a0c"}, {"id": "832c10", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a0d"}, {"id": "b77622", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a0e"}, {"id": "65c114", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a0f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a10", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8a74"], "question": {"text": "<p>The pressure of a gas changes linearly with volume from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;as shown in figure. If no heat is supplied to or extracted from the gas then change in the internal energy of the gas will be</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ffa24b284-3656-46d6-b32d-f5188b3835dc-9895800_1.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 309px; height: 260px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "6bc165", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a11"}, {"id": "d7a797", "text": "Zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a12"}, {"id": "384a5c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a13"}, {"id": "962108", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a14"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a15", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475d"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4713"], "question": {"text": "For a diatomic gas, if $\\gamma_1=\\left(\\frac{C p}{C v}\\right)$ for rigid molecules and $\\gamma_2=\\left(\\frac{C p}{C v}\\right)$ for another diatomic molecules, but also having vibrational modes. Then, which one of the following options is correct ? (Cp and Cv are specific heats of the gas at constant pressure and volume)"}, "options": [{"id": "5fa25e", "text": "$\\gamma_2=\\gamma_1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a16"}, {"id": "1a9443", "text": "$2 \\gamma_2=\\gamma_1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a17"}, {"id": "adb610", "text": "$\\gamma_2 \\lt \\gamma_1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a18"}, {"id": "924437", "text": "$\\gamma_2\\gt\\gamma_1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a19"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a1a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9938"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match the thermodynamics processes taking place in a system with the correct conditions. In the table : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>is the heat supplied, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>W</mi></math> is the work done and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi></math> is change in internal energy of the system.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 350px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>Process</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>Condition</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(I)</td>\t\t\t<td>Adiabatic</td>\t\t\t<td>(A)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(II)</td>\t\t\t<td>Isothermal</td>\t\t\t<td>(B)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(III)</td>\t\t\t<td>Isochoric</td>\t\t\t<td>(C)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(IV)</td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>Isobaric</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t\t<td>(D)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>"}, "options": [{"id": "467ea7", "text": "(I) - (A), (II) - (B), (III) - (D), (IV) - (D)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a1b"}, {"id": "10ab44", "text": "(I) - (B), (II) - (A), (III) - (D), (IV) - (C)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a1c"}, {"id": "fcdd73", "text": "(I) - (A), (II) - (A), (III) - (B), (IV) - (C)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a1d"}, {"id": "699ade", "text": "(I) - (B), (II) - (D), (III) - (A), (IV) - (C)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a1e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a1f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["6162fb026ed13040ec84a084"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p><strong>Statement I:</strong> If heat is added to a system, its temperature must increase.</p><p><strong>Statement II:</strong> If positive work is done by a system in a thermodynamic process, its volume must increase.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "8ca0af", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a20"}, {"id": "a1448d", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a21"}, {"id": "f388ed", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a22"}, {"id": "297d80", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a23"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a24", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475d"], "concepts": ["6162fb026ed13040ec84a08f"], "question": {"text": "An ideal gas goes from an initial state to final state. During the process, the pressure of gas increases linearly with temperature.\nA. The work done by gas during the process is zero.\nB. The heat added to gas is different from change in its internal energy.\nC. The volume of the gas is increased.\nD. The internal energy of the gas is increased.\nE. The process is isochoric (constant volume process)\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "1bd6bc", "text": "E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a25"}, {"id": "49101a", "text": "A, B, C, D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a26"}, {"id": "69dffe", "text": "A, D, E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a27"}, {"id": "ec7464", "text": "A, C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a28"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a29", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6117bc0067dbe2603c3ec296"], "question": {"text": "A cylinder with fixed capacity of <math><mn>67.2</mn></math> litre contains helium gas at STP. The amount of heat needed to raise the temperature of the gas by <math><mn>20</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is:<br />[Given that <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.31</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "1affd8", "text": "<math><mn>748</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a2a"}, {"id": "449045", "text": "<math><mn>700</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a2b"}, {"id": "3915cc", "text": "<math><mn>350</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a2c"}, {"id": "08a15d", "text": "<math><mn>374</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a2d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a2e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4739"], "question": {"text": "<p>A thermodynamic system is taken from an original state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> to an intermediate state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> by a linear process as shown in the figure. Its volume is then reduced to the original value from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> by an isobaric process. The total work done by the gas from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> would be :</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F2a96272b-4254-4cee-84b3-193b8206f736.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 222px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "fc11ce", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>33800</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a2f"}, {"id": "8fc9c8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2200</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a30"}, {"id": "bbb36c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a31"}, {"id": "78cf49", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a32"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a33", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6162fb046ed13040ec84a191"], "question": {"text": "Starting with the same initial conditions, an ideal gas expands from volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in three different ways. The work done by the gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> if the process is purely isothermal, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, if the process is purely adiabatic and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> if the process is purely&nbsp;isobaric. Then, choose the correct option"}, "options": [{"id": "029a76", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a34"}, {"id": "3a2335", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a35"}, {"id": "e34398", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a36"}, {"id": "502b86", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a37"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a38", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba3"], "question": {"text": "<p>For a perfect gas, two pressures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are shown in figure. The graph shows</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F81730a84-d2b5-488f-8df0-7095da14b460-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 195px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "feb401", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a39"}, {"id": "9f9695", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a3a"}, {"id": "0c3943", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a3b"}, {"id": "6e8a48", "text": "Insufficient data to draw any conclusion", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a3c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a3d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c7"], "question": {"text": "<p>Thermodynamic process is shown below on a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;diagram for one mole of an ideal gas. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, then the ratio of temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc12f95f7-47c6-427c-8bcf-2fb390575cba-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 196px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "cdcefa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a3e"}, {"id": "e2940a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a3f"}, {"id": "1a5379", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a40"}, {"id": "4711da", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a41"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a42", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8a74"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>08</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math> air is heated at constant volume through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The specific heat of air at constant volume is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>17</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kcal</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mo>°</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>18</mn><mo> </mo><mi>joule</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>cal</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The change in its internal energy is approximately."}, "options": [{"id": "723ebc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>318</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef5c677dc36a88f2a43"}, {"id": "9fed4a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo> </mo><mi ma