44a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c7"], "question": {"text": "The change in the magnitude of the volume of an ideal gas when a small additional pressure&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> is applied at a constant temperature, is the same as the change when the temperature is reduced by a small quantity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>&nbsp;at constant pressure. The initial temperature and pressure of the gas were <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively. If&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>&#916;T</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>|</mo><mi>&#916;P</mi><mo>|</mo></math>&nbsp;then value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>atm</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;is __________"}, "options": [{"id": "9ea7a7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a75"}, {"id": "f158bd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a76"}, {"id": "a3caf8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a77"}, {"id": "986d61", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a78"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a79", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475d"], "concepts": ["6162fb026ed13040ec84a08f"], "question": {"text": "A container is divided into two chambers by a partition. The volume of first chamber is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>litre</mi></math> and second chamber is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>litre</mi></math>. The first chamber contain <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math> moles of gas at pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math>&nbsp;and second chamber contain <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math> moles of gas at pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math>. After the partition is removed and the mixture attains equilibrium, then, the common equilibrium pressure existing in the mixture is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math>. Value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;(nearest integer) is&nbsp;<u>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</u>"}, "options": [{"id": "d254ca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a7a"}, {"id": "fd2d85", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a7b"}, {"id": "a78fb5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a7c"}, {"id": "f9db31", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a7d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f2a7e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e808d"], "question": {"text": "At a certain temperature, the degrees of freedom per molecule for gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>. The gas 